              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "The address you entered\u2014`mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx`\u2014is a **legacy URL** previously used by the Georgia Department of Revenue's Motor Vehicle Division (MVD) for online vehicle registration and license plate (tag) renewals. \n\nIf you are trying to renew your tags, apply for a title, or manage your vehicle registrations in Georgia, you should use the updated and current systems:\n\n### 1. The Current Official Portal: Georgia DRIVES e-Services\nThe State of Georgia has transitioned all of its motor vehicle online services to the **Georgia DRIVES** platform:\n*   **Official Website:** [Georgia DRIVES e-Services (drives.mvd.dor.ga.gov)](https://drives.mvd.dor.ga.gov/)\n\n### 2. Manage Your Vehicles with MyMVD\nThe Georgia Department of Revenue offers a platform called **MyMVD**. By creating an account, you can manage all of your vehicles in one place.\n*   **What it does:** Once logged in, you can view your registered vehicles and request services (like replacing a title or renewing tags) without needing to manually re-enter your VIN, license plate number, or driver's license number every time.\n*   **Where to access:** You can sign up or log in directly through the [Georgia DRIVES Portal](https://drives.mvd.dor.ga.gov/).\n\n### What you can do on the new Georgia DRIVES portal:\n*   **Renew Vehicle Registration (Tags):** Pay your annual registration fees and renew your license plate decals online.\n*   **Check Vehicle Status:** Look up your registration, TAVT (Title Ad Valorem Tax) estimates, and insurance status.\n*   **Pre-File Title & Registration Applications:** Complete forms online before going to your local county tag office to save time.\n*   **Vanity & Specialty Plates:** Search available designs and check the availability of custom prestige (vanity) license plates.\n*   **Cancel Registration:** Voluntarily cancel your vehicle's registration online if it is sold, inoperable, or stored (to prevent insurance lapse fines).",
